In article <1991May2.065431.3570@phoenix.pub.uu.oz.au> grue@phoenix.pub.uu.oz.au (Adam Eberbach) writes:
>Okay....this is getting annoying. I have recently started to play 
>Nethack, after playing The Software Distillery's Hacklite (Amiga)
>for years. I liked Hacklite for its bullet-proof nature and its cute
>color graphics, but it has none of the features of Nethack 3.0 patch 10.
>Magic markers, oracles, statues, spellbooks etc. are just some of the 
>things missing.
> 
>Nethack looked great, after reading this group for a while, so I started
>playing, but I can't get ANYWHERE. I like Wizards, or Rogues.
>
>My main problems are these - 
> 
>1. I can't uncurse spellbooks - what do I have to do, wield them then 
>   read "remove curse" or make them +1?

Well, there are lots of ways to uncurse. Some, like reading ordinary
remove curse scrolls, work only for weapons you're wielding and
things you're wearing. You can dip the cursed thing in a fountain,
but there are bad effects: scrolls and potions are ruined, and
you might summon a monster. Praying usually only uncurses if your
god is VERY pleased with you (I once got hunger fixed, all my hitpoints
restored, all my cursed stuff uncursed and something blessed all
from one prayer) because some other "more serious" problem is fixed
first. Finally, dipping in holy water works for everything but you
might not want to waste holy water on the cursed thing in question.

>2. The gods HATE me! I never pray more than once every 400 moves or so,
>   sometimes even less, but they have NEVER given me a wish. I have 
>   also only had my weapon blessed twice, in at least 100 games. (Yes 
>   I have been good - no robbing, or killing my cat)

I don't pray for wishes or to have my weapon blessed. Pray to save
your life, and keep that to a minimum. As far as I know neither robbing
shops nor killing your pet affects your god's opinion of you.

>3. Apart from spellbooks, I can't uncurse anything else.

See question 1.

>4. Even in -X plore mode, I can't get Mjollnir or any of the other
>   named weapons. I'm aware of alignment constraints, but I can't get 
>   ANYTHING! I have been typing 'Mjollnir' or 'Excalibur' when prompted - 
>   is this the right syntax?

Syntax for wishing? No. Type it as it would appear in your inventory:
a long sword named Excalibur, perhaps. Though you can get Excalibur by
dipping a long sword in a fountain. I don't wish for artifacts, though:
rather I offer at altars (no praying) until one appears for me.

>5. I get ridiculously small hit point totals - on 10th level I am usually
>   getting about 55-70 hp. My constitution is usually between 10 and 14,
>   not high, but shouldn't I be getting more than this?

No idea. Quaffing a potion of extra healing bumps your max hitpoints.
Taking fire damage drops your max hitpoints.

>6. So far the best weapon I have found is a (non-blessed) +4 dwarven
>   short sword, which I nearly died in the process of getting (the dwarf
>   didn't want to let go). Where are all the neat things like longswords
>   and polearms and maces that Hacklite had?

I've seen all of these. Patience...


